Package: csvschema
Title: Self-Describing CSV Files with Embedded, Loss-Tolerant Schemas
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Jesse", "Lecy", email = "jdlecy@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Writes and reads CSV files that carry their own schema inside
    ordinary data columns, so the file opens as a plain CSV in every tool and
    the schema survives sorting, filtering, row loss, encoding changes, and
    spreadsheet round-trips. A table schema (field names, types, formats,
    missing codes, factor levels, keys) is packetized into short ASCII tokens
    and spread redundantly through '_schema' columns; the schema is recovered
    from any surviving subset of rows, verified, and applied on read. A
    '_canary' column stores fragile sample values per variable so corruption of
    the data itself is detected and diagnosed. An optional Frictionless
    'datapackage.json' sidecar cross-checks the in-band schema.
